WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.759
Week 2: Greetings and First Contact. greet and take leave introduce yourself and another person choose tú or usted

2
00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:15.711
Cultural lens. Greetings, personal space, titles, and cheek-kissing conventions vary by country and relationship.

3
00:00:15.711 --> 00:00:27.569
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:39.192
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.192 --> 00:00:48.021
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.021 --> 00:01:11.359
Model language. Hola, me llamo Alex. — Hello, my name is Alex. Mucho gusto, señora Rivera. — Nice to meet you, Mrs. Rivera. ¿Cómo te llamas? — What is your name? Le presento a mi compañera. — Let me introduce you to my classmate. Nos vemos mañana; que tenga buen día. — See you tomorrow; have a good day.

7
00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:21.107
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
